## Enable RoCE drivers

If your compute resources support RoCE, the following commands add the same
RDMA stack to the compute image. If you enabled InfiniBand drivers above, the
stack is already there and the script skips the install.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Add RoCE (RDMA) drivers to compute image -->
<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_roce -->
<!-- ohpc_if [[ ${enable_ib} -ne 1 ]] -->
```bash
# Add RDMA support
{{ compute_group_install("InfiniBand Support") }}
```
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->
{% if is_warewulf %}

If you set `${roce_mtu}`, the following gives the computes' provisioning
interface the same MTU as the *head node*'s internal interface.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Optionally set the RoCE MTU on compute nodes -->
<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_roce -->
<!-- ohpc_if [[ -n "${roce_mtu}" ]] -->
```bash
wwctl profile set -y nodes --netname=default --mtu="${roce_mtu}"
```
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->
{% endif %}

To run MPI over RoCE, select the RDMA device and port for UCX, for example
`UCX_NET_DEVICES=mlx5_1:1`; `rdma link` lists each RDMA device with its network
interface.
